<p>One thing I surmised from the way it was written (others seem to have this impression) is that the box, once closed, then becomes the alternate reality. Whoever's inside is trapped there, the only exit to &quot;space&quot;. Unless a third party opens the box from outside. Might also stress earlier in the description it is bigger on the inside. I didn't catch that until the logs.</p>
</div>
